Personally I've found Sam to be as easy as Bar or Val; granted, the
Valk quest is easier and their quest artifact is great, but by the time
you get to the quest you're pretty much past all the hardest parts of
the game anyway (except maybe for monks), though you need to be
somewhat careful facing the Tsurugi.  (IMO, the 1/2 damage thing would
be a lot more useful for a role that isn't swimming in hp already)

The valk gets a +1 long sword vs. a +0 katana; that's a minor win for
the valk (washes out to the sword being +1 damage against large
monsters and identical otherwise), but it makes dipping for Excalibur a
virtual guarantee for lawful valks once they can take on demons/snakes.
 Samurai have to hope to find one.

Early speed is a _big_ win for a wombat, enough to basically offset the
+3 shield for a good while.  And getting a decent missile weapon early
on helps if you're not doing strictly melee wombatism.



